  "principles": [
    "An interpreter decision is authoritative only when its inputs, evidence, alternatives, selected rule and transition are digest-bound.",
    "A role return may preserve or reduce scope, but may not change the selected target or authorize an automatic retry.",
    "A 9.7 role score is not a certification without disjoint independent holdout evidence and zero generated function stubs.",
    "L0 and L1 self-development requires a baseline-versus-candidate experiment with no metric or role regression.",
    "Existing local corpus must be deduplicated and split before targeted external acquisition is allowed.",
    "Prospective errors are evaluated from the latest post-cutoff snapshot of each project; a later clean report retracts stale project evidence.",
    "Declared distribution scripts are project-identity evidence and must not depend on CLI tokens in a repository name.",
    "Declared project-owned plugin entry points outrank incidental parser or CLI signals when classifying project identity.",
    "Artifact presence, target continuity and a recognized project never create a role score; semantic role evidence is required.",
    "Structural artifact completeness is diagnostic only; validated role scores require causal diagnosis, a defect-specific repair design, an executable implementation delta, and downstream outcome evidence.",
    "Project archetype ground truth is part of Project Analyzer holdout scoring; a correct broad stratum cannot hide an incorrect project identity.",
    "Project identity and strong source-contract evidence outrank incidental internal capabilities during archetype selection.",
    "Pytest subtest nodeids, class methods and local wildcard re-exports must remain target-bindable, while fixture setup failures cannot grant repair authority.",
    "Failure-repair specifications must replace stale generic requirements, acceptance traceability and verification plans with one target-bound contract.",
    "Repository lineage and source ownership are separate evidence dimensions; a holdout needs independent owners in every promoted project stratum.",
    "Verification-only execution proves callable acceptance, not project development or architecture quality.",
    "Unknown project clusters remain research candidates and never promote automatically.",
    "Broad Python project strata remain development debt after narrow-role semantic revalidation.",
    "Web UI is deferred until the architecture and authority contracts are stable.",
    "A verification result with no executed checks and no executable acceptance evidence is not verified and cannot be treated as success.",
    "A durable worker may mutate a running job only while it holds the unique lease token for the current attempt.",
    "Runtime safety evidence cannot substitute for a same-task product comparison against a direct agent and a shortened role chain.",
    "A defect-driven role chain must preserve one digest-bound ProblemOutcomeContract from baseline evidence through Reviewer; artifact completeness cannot replace causal conformance.",
    "A consumed training replay may demonstrate chain competence but its structural score cannot remove training caps or substitute for a fresh owner-independent holdout."
  ],
